      "summaries": {
        "en": "SAM3 is a video segmentation model that automatically identifies and tracks objects across video frames, solving the labor-intensive task of manual video annotation. It builds on the SAM architecture by incorporating temporal consistency mechanisms, enabling it to maintain object identity across frames even with occlusions or motion blur. Researchers can use it for video analysis tasks like activity recognition or autonomous driving simulations by feeding video clips and receiving frame-by-frame segmentation masks.",
        "zh": "SAM3是一个视频分割模型，能够自动识别并跟踪视频中的物体，解决了传统手动标注视频的繁琐问题。它在SAM架构基础上引入了时序一致性机制，通过跨帧特征关联保持物体身份连续性，即使遇到遮挡或运动模糊也能稳定追踪。研究人员可将视频片段输入模型，获取逐帧的分割掩码，用于行为分析、自动驾驶模拟等场景，为动态视觉理解提供高效工具。",
        "es": "SAM3 is a video segmentation model that automatically identifies and tracks objects across video frames, solving the labor-intensive task of manual video annotation. It builds on the SAM architecture by incorporating temporal consistency mechanisms, enabling it to maintain object identity across frames even with occlusions or motion blur. Researchers can use it for video analysis tasks like activity recognition or autonomous driving simulations by feeding video clips and receiving frame-by-frame segmentation masks.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "sam3 stands out for transformers, safetensors, and sam3_video in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "SAM3 is a video segmentation model that automatically identifies and tracks objects across video frames, solving the labor-intensive task of manual video annotation. It builds on the SAM architecture by incorporating temporal consistency mechanisms, enabling it to maintain object identity across frames even with occlusions or motion blur. Researchers can use it for video analysis tasks like activity recognition or autonomous driving simulations by feeding video clips and receiving frame-by-frame segmentation masks.",
          "how": "Review https://huggingface.co/facebook/sam3 for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
